    {
      "document_id": "knowledge_ccfd8ffc98d867f9da49fdef7ad645f30925ca381483fb25e8a305c146a2adf7",
      "text": "---\nkb_version: kb_v2\nsource_type: primary_regulatory\nsource_file: RBI-FRAUD-RISK-MANAGEMENT-15-07-24.pdf\nsource_pages: [13, 14]\nsynthetic: false\n---\n\n# RBI 2024 Fraud Category\n\n## Category\n\nWilful falsification, destruction, alteration or mutilation of records with intent to defraud.\n\n## Source position\n\nThis category appears in the RBI 2024 fraud-reporting taxonomy. It should be selected only when the facts of a case support the category under the applicable reporting framework.\n\n## Important boundary\n\nThe presence of a transaction alert in this project does not by itself establish that this regulatory fraud category applies. The ML alert and later investigation are separate from formal classification/reporting.\n\n## Retrieval use\n\nUseful for questions asking:\n- What fraud category may be relevant?\n- What terminology does RBI use for this category?\n- Which reporting taxonomy entry corresponds to a described fact pattern?\n\nPrimary source: RBI Master Direction on Fraud Risk Management, 15 July 2024.",
